      "topic": "atr_percentile_method",
      "choice": "Computed the 20th-percentile cutoff of the trailing 252-bar ATR window (current bar included) via statistics.quantiles(data, n=5)[0], and required current ATR >= that cutoff to pass the filter.",
      "reason": "Spec states a percentile-rank filter but does not name a computation method; this is a standard, literal reading of 'bottom 20th percentile over the last 252 bars.'"
    },
    {
      "topic": "atr_percentile_warmup",
      "choice": "No entries are taken until a full 252-bar ATR history has accumulated inside the strategy (in addition to backtrader's automatic ~200-bar indicator minperiod from SMA(200)).",
      "reason": "The 252-bar percentile lookback is a manual statistic, not a built-in indicator, so it has no automatic minperiod; entries can only start once the window is genuinely full, which is the closest literal implementation of the stated lookback."
    },
    {
      "topic": "capital_definition",
      "choice": "'Capital' in the 2% floating-loss rule is the initial starting portfolio value, captured once via self.broker.getvalue() in __init__ (i.e., the $10,000 starting cash), not fluctuating current equity.",
      "reason": "Spec doesn't define 'capital'; a fixed reference is the more standard reading for a per-trade risk cap and avoids the threshold drifting with unrelated equity changes."
    },
    {
